      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Grief often strips us of our old identity, making it difficult to recognize the person we were before those connections ended. It is not pointless to mourn a version of yourself simply because that person has passed; the struggle you feel proves you still care enough to ache. Please consider reaching out to a trusted friend or mental health professional, as this emotional weight needs a safe place to land.",
